{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790452169,"nonce":"idSuL8SLbwpah1uhmhSkycwnJK8=","title":"A project file: \u003cname\u003e.cbproj declares languages, entry, dependencies and plugins","message":"Today the driver infers a project: the entry is always a .hl the user\ncompiled (Haxe with -lib caribou), the roots are the class paths of the\n.hxml files (else src), a language is present when a file of its\nextension is (a .py brings Python), plugins are whatever sits in\nplugins/ beside the program, and Wren packages come from a hatchfile.\nUser direction (2026-09-26): one project file declares all of it.\nDecided with the user:\n- `\u003cname\u003e.cbproj`, TOML, one per project. `caribou run` and `caribou\n  build` with no argument find the one in the directory.\n- The entry is a module in any language. caribou runs the Haxe compiler\n  (with -lib caribou) itself: no hand-written .hxml, no prebuilt .hl.\n- It replaces .hxml and hatchfile as caribou's configuration. A\n  hatchfile inside a Wren package still describes that package for hatch.\n\nDraft schema:\n\n    [project]\n    name = \"game\"\n    entry = \"haxe:game.Main\"        # language:module\n\n    [languages.haxe]\n    roots = [\"src\"]\n    libs = [\"heaps\"]                # haxelibs; caribou's own is implied\n    [languages.wren]\n    roots = [\"src\"]\n    [languages.python]\n    roots = [\"src\"]\n    [languages.zynml]\n    grammar = \"grammars/zynml.zyn\"  # a Zyntax language by its grammar\n    roots = [\"src\"]\n\n    [dependencies]                  # Wren hatch packages\n    \"@hatch:greet\" = { path = \"../greet\" }\n\n    [plugins]                       # native plugins, by library\n    gpu = { path = \"plugins/libcaribou_gpu\" }\n\n    [target.wasm32-wasip1]          # per-target settings, when needed\n\nNamespaces stay as today: the first directory under a root (src/game is\ngame). Output goes to target/ beside the file: \u003cname\u003e.cb for a bundle,\n\u003cname\u003e.wasm for an AOT target.\n\nPhases:\n1. Parse and find the file (driver); `caribou run` / `build` with none\n   given use it.\n2. Compile a Haxe entry: haxe -cp \u003croots\u003e -lib caribou -lib \u003clibs\u003e\n   -main \u003cmodule\u003e -hl target/\u003cname\u003e.hl.\n3. Roots, languages and Zyntax frontends from the file, not inferred.\n4. Wren packages from [dependencies], not a hatchfile.\n5. Plugins from [plugins], not plugins/ beside the program.\n6. An entry in another language: the session starts a Wren, Lua or\n   Python main.\n7. The Haxe macro (-lib caribou) reads the same file for its roots.","files":null}]}